From 8a9fa9cc8c0fbd239530b0fbc571bc8320aab1ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:55:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] runtime: GA2_FPS high frame rate clock, presentation per
 flip, frame-timing oracle trace

A second scheduler clock (FrameTick, fps*1000/1001 Hz, cycle- and host-paced like the
VBLANK) that the game's RenderFlip waits on instead of WaitVSync (hooks in the game
overrides); the GS scans out at the ticks while the game waits on it, the window loop
shows every new frame (readback ring notifies, no 60 Hz cap, vsync swap interval).
Native mode (GA2_FPS unset or 60) is unchanged.

Oracle support (GA2_FRAMETRACE): trace writer, frame fingerprints and PNG shots, IOP
key-on / CD read / RPC observers (iop_trace.h, kept out of iop_host.h), scripted pad
(GA2_PAD_SCRIPT through the game hooks), GA2_FIXED_CLOCK (frozen CDVD RTC so runs are
deterministic), per-thread CPU in the [ga2 fps] report.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
